  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tMTD IT\n\t\tMTD IT\n\n### MTD IT - Linking the Sole Traders and Individuals in Bulk\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Mon, 15 Jun, 2026 at  9:54 AM\n\n\t\tThis article explains how to link sole traders and individuals within the MTD IT module. Linking is a mandatory requirement when using the Bookkeeping module alongside the MTD IT module.\n\nThis feature allows you to link multiple individuals across multiple sole trader businesses. There are two scenarios to be aware of:\n\nLinking different individuals across different sole trader businesses.\nAssigning the same individual across multiple sole trader businesses.\n\nScenario 1: Assigning Multiple Individuals Across Multiple Sole Traders\n\nUse this scenario when you need to assign different individuals to different sole trader businesses.\n\nNavigation > Capium 365 Client Portal > Manage > Clients\n\nFollow the steps below:\n\nStep 1 - Navigate to the Capium 365 Client Portal.\n\nStep 2 - Open the Manage section.\n\nStep 3 - Select your list of clients.\n\nStep 4 - Once the relevant clients are selected, click Assign Individual at the bottom of the screen.\n\nStep 5 - On the pop-up screen, you can allocate an existing individual or add a new one by typing their name into the blank field provided.\n\nScenario 2: Assigning One Individual Across Multiple Sole Traders\n\nUse this scenario when you need to link one individual to several sole trader businesses.\n\nNavigation > Capium 365 Client Portal > Manage > Clients\n\nFollow the steps below:\n\nStep 1 - Navigate to the Capium 365 Client Portal.\n\nStep 2 - Open the Manage section.\n\nStep 3 - Select your list of clients.\n\nStep 4 - Select the multiple sole trader businesses that need to be linked to one individual.\n\nStep 5 - On the pop-up screen, select the option Assign one individual to all businesses.\n\nStep 6 - Select the individual you wish to assign and confirm the selection to apply them across all chosen businesses.\n\nPlease Note: Once a sole trader and individual record are linked, they share a single licence. You will still see two records across 365, My Admin, and Practice Management — this is expected, as they remain separate legal entities. \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
  "bodyHtml": "\n\t<div class=\"breadcrumb\">\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions\"> Solution home </a>\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions/9000118618\">MTD IT</a>\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions/folders/9000201911\">MTD IT</a>\n\t</div>\n\t<b class=\"page-stamp page-stamp-article\">\n\t\t<b class=\"icon-page-article\"></b>\n\t</b>\n\n\t<h2 class=\"heading\">MTD IT - Linking the Sole Traders and Individuals in Bulk\n\t \t<a href=\"#\"\n            class=\"solution-print--icon print--remove\"\n \t\t\ttitle=\"Print this Article\"\n \t\t\tarial-role=\"link\"\n \t\t\tarial-label=\"Print this Article\"\n\t\t\tid=\"print-article\"\n \t\t>\n\t\t\t<span class=\"icon-print\"></span>\n\t\t\t<span class=\"text-print\">Print</span>\n \t\t</a>\n\t</h2>\n\t\n\t<p>Modified on: Mon, 15 Jun, 2026 at  9:54 AM</p>\n\t<hr />\n\t\n\n\t<article class=\"article-body\" id=\"article-body\" rel=\"image-enlarge\">\n\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\">This article explains how to link sole traders and individuals within the MTD IT module. Linking is a mandatory requirement when using the Bookkeeping module alongside the MTD IT module.</span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This feature allows you to link multiple individuals across multiple sole trader businesses. There are two scenarios to be aware of:</span></span></p><ol style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><li style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Linking different individuals across different sole trader businesses.</span></span></li><li style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Assigning the same individual across multiple sole trader businesses.</span></span></li></ol><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br><strong>Scenario 1: Assigning Multiple Individuals Across Multiple Sole Traders</strong></span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Use this scenario when you need to assign different individuals to different sole trader businesses.</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Navigation &gt; Capium 365 Client Portal &gt; Manage &gt; Clients</strong></span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Follow the steps below:</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Step 1</strong> - Navigate to the Capium 365 Client Portal.</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Step 2</strong> - Open the <strong>Manage</strong> section.</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Step 3</strong> - Select your list of clients.</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Step 4</strong> - Once the relevant clients are selected, click <strong>Assign Individual</strong> at the bottom of the screen.</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Step 5</strong> - On the pop-up screen, you can allocate an existing individual or add a new one by typing their name into the blank field provided.</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/9248545485/original/Xe2x3n7_WizmB5ZtpL4VIbsqUJOFFQzaWA.gif?1778752146\" style=\"width: auto; max-width: 100%;\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"9248545485\"></span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br><br><strong>Scenario 2: Assigning One Individual Across Multiple Sole Traders</strong></span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Use this scenario when you need to link one individual to several sole trader businesses.</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Navigation &gt; Capium 365 Client Portal &gt; Manage &gt; Clients</strong></span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Follow the steps below:</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Step 1</strong> - Navigate to the Capium 365 Client Portal.</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Step 2</strong> - Open the <strong>Manage</strong> section.</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Step 3</strong> - Select your list of clients.</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Step 4</strong> - Select the multiple sole trader businesses that need to be linked to one individual.</span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Step 5</strong> - On the pop-up screen, select the option <strong>Assign one individual to all businesses</strong>.</span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><strong>Step 6</strong> - Select the individual you wish to assign and confirm the selection to apply them across all chosen businesses.</span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/9248545901/original/Te5Ug5QVVPv7jVXvO_MMryZ4qco3q2IE0A.gif?1778752771\" style=\"width: auto; max-width: 100%;\" class=\"fr-fil fr-dib\" data-attachment=\"[object Object]\" data-id=\"9248545901\"></span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><br></span></span></p><p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span class=\"fr-view collab-annotatable\" data-test-id=\"article-description\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; overflow-wrap: break-word; color: rgb(18, 51, 76); font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; position: relative; display: block; cursor: auto;\"></span></span></span></p><div class=\"OutlineElement Ltr SCXW204744369 BCX0\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; word-break: normal; overflow-wrap: break-word; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); -webkit-user-drag: none; -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; user-select: text; clear: both; cursor: text; overflow: visible; position: relative; direction: ltr; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; whi